'''Hawkins Cookers Limited''' Inc and formerly known as '''Pressure Cookers and Appliances Ltd''',<ref name="Hawkins Cookers Ltd. (HAWKINCOOK) - Company History"/> is an Indian company which manufactures [[pressure cookers]] and [[cookware]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.hawkinscookers.com/6.0.contact.html |title=Contact us |publisher=Hawkinscookers.com |access-date=23 November 2010}}</ref> The company is based in [[Mumbai]] and has three manufacturing plants at [[Thane]], [[Hoshiarpur]] and [[Jaunpur, Uttar Pradesh|Jaunpur]]. It manufactures under brand names of Hawkins, Futura, Contura, Hevibase, Big Boy, Miss Mary and Ventura. Hawkins is one of the largest pressure cooker manufacturers in India and exports its products to more than 65 countries.<ref>{{cite book |title=Enterprise Resource Planning: Concepts and Practice |last=Garg |first=Vinod Kumar /Atibal Singh|author2=Venkitakrishnan, N. K. |year=2004 |publisher=Prentice Hall of India |isbn=81-203-2254-1 |page=138 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=5mNjGObvTaAC&dq=%22Hawkins+Cookers%22&pg=PA138 }}</ref>

==History==
Hawkins Cookers was started in 1959 by H. D. Vasudeva as Pressure Cookers and Appliances Ltd, in technical collaboration with [[L G Hawkins & Co Ltd]] of England.<ref name="The man who made brand Hawkins">{{cite web|url=https://www.moneycontrol.com/news/business/companies/brahm-vasudeva-the-man-who-made-brand-hawkins-synonymous-with-core-focus-5541211.html |title=Brahm Vasudeva: The man who made brand Hawkins synonymous with core focus|author=M Saraswathy |publisher=moneycontrol.com |date=11 September 2020}}</ref> L G Hawkins and Company Limited was founded by Leonard George Hawkins in 1913 and manufactured home appliances.<ref name="Consumer Products Domestic Appliances">{{cite web|url=https://www.pye-story.org/companies/consumer-products/domestic-appliances |title=Consumer Products Domestic Appliances|publisher=pye-story.org|access-date=5 January 2022}}</ref><ref name="L G Hawkins Ltd">{{cite web|url=https://www.pye-story.org/companies/research-section/l-g-hawkins-ltd |title=LG Hawkins & Co Ltd|publisher=pye-story.org|access-date=5 January 2022}}</ref>

The company was initially known as Pressure Cookers and Appliances Ltd and manufactured and marketed of Hawkins pressure cooker under agreement with [[L G Hawkins & Co Ltd]] of England. In 1986, the company acquired the present name.<ref name="Hawkins Cookers Ltd. (HAWKINCOOK) - Company History">{{cite web|url=https://www.business-standard.com/company/hawkins-cookers-451/information/company-history|title=Hawkins Cookers History|publisher=business-standard.com |access-date=6 January 2022}}</ref>

L G Hawkins and Company Limited was bought by [[Pye Ltd.]] in 1939.<ref name="Consumer Products Domestic Appliances"/><ref name="Pye Commercial Growth">{{cite web|url=https://www.pye-story.org/history/commercial-growth |title=Commercial Growth|publisher=pye-story.org|access-date=5 January 2022}}</ref> In 1962, Pye acquired [[EKCO|Ekco & Co Ltd]] and L G Hawkins was merged with similar Ekco activities to form Ekco Hawkins and later Ekco Hastings.<ref name="Consumer Products Domestic Appliances"/> Pye was later acquired by [[Philips]] in 1986.<ref name="History Acquisition by Philips">{{cite web |title=Commercial Growth. Acquisition by Philips |url=https://www.pye-story.org/history/acquisition-by-philips |access-date=5 January 2022 |publisher=pye-story.org}}</ref> Ekco-Hawkins later became [[Philips]] Small Domestic Appliances Product Division and products were rebadged as Philips, but was closed down in the late 1998, due to overseas competition and Philips global rationalization.<ref name="L G Hawkins Ltd"/> The Hawkins Universal trademark was acquired by Hawkins Cookers Ltd in 1986<ref name="ManufacturersL G Hawkins">{{cite news |url=https://www.teasmade.uk/l-g-hawkins/ |title=L Hawkins |newspaper=Teasmade |date=October 2015 |publisher=teasmade.uk |access-date=6 January 2022 |archive-date=6 January 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220106171415/https://www.teasmade.uk/l-g-hawkins/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref name="Hawkins Cookers History">{{cite web|url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/hawkins-cookers-ltd/infocompanyhistory/companyid-13632.cms |title=Hawkins Cookers History|publisher=economictimes.indiatimes.com |access-date=6 January 2022}}</ref> and company name was changed from Pressure Cookers & Appliances Ltd to Hawkins Cookers Ltd.<ref name="Hawkins Cookers Ltd. (HAWKINCOOK) - Company History"/><ref name="Hawkins Cookers History"/>

The company is traded on the [[Bombay Stock Exchange]] under the symbol HWKN. It has raised funds through "fixed deposits", a term for high-interest term deposits issued by industrial companies rather than banks.

Hawkins has sold over 110 million pressure cookers worldwide. Today, it makes 88 different models of pressure cookers in 13 different types. All Hawkins pressure cookers are listed by Underwriters Laboratories Inc., USA, an independent institution testing products for public safety. Hawkins pressure cookers feature an inside-fitting lid, which cannot be opened until the steam pressure inside the cooker falls to a safe level. Hawkins was listed as India's most trusted kitchen appliances brand by The Brand Trust Report 2015.<ref>{{Cite book|title = The Brand Trust Report India Study 2015|last = Chandramouli|publisher = TRA|year = 2015|isbn = 978-81-920823-8-7|pages = 156–157}}</ref>

